// The arr_elem_table "max 512" limit is documented and sized per function.
// On the IR path it was never reset between functions, so it was really a
// PROGRAM-WIDE budget -- and the diagnostic names neither the function nor the
// fact that the count is cumulative, so a program that grew past it looked
// like a program with one impossible function in it.
//
// 20 functions, 30 local arrays each. No function is anywhere near 512; the
// program totals 600. Before the reset in ir_lower_function this failed to
// compile with "error: arr_elem_table overflow (max 512)".
//
// GENERATED SHAPE, checked by arithmetic: each function returns its first
// array's element, which holds f * 30, so the sum over f in 0..19 is
// 30 * (19 * 20 / 2) = 5700. A compile that merely stops erroring is not
// enough -- the sum proves the arrays still scale and store correctly.

